The five log scans (three no_errors, two checksum_errors) give 0.93 verified. Submitting "verified" now has an expected loss of about 4.1, against 8 for escalating. No cached tool has been called, so the staleness belief stays at the 0.33 prior.

Each remaining call is worth making, with backup_status the best. A stale replica mostly says "verified", so a non-verified report from the cache is informative. backup_status is slightly more accurate than backup_console when the replica is fresh. I'll call backup_status with my last unit.

