One `all_noerror` reading moves my estimate to about 79% resolving, 12% intermittent and 8% failing. Submitting "resolving" now would carry an expected loss of about 12 (0.21 × 60), which is too high.

`query_log_sample` is never stale, and its errors are independent across calls. Repeated samples therefore give fresh evidence at 1 unit each, while `dig_probe` costs 4. I'll take another sample.

